  The squirrel has no opinion on whether desire for children will fall away
from transhumanity -- that's possibly up to the trans-humans.  However,
very advanced societies (and individuals) are potentially enormous consumers
of diverse resources.  Such entities might find useful some form of
behavior that limited reproduction and/or growth in the event of shortage.
Extropians confident of Boundless Expansion would likely regard any such
shortages as transient, local phenomena, but even in such cases a temporary
non-expansive response might be useful.
  Several kinds of terran creatures that are capable of being serious drains
