The effect is likely to be just the opposite: those who are literate
are able to tap into great resources, while those who are not will be
cut off.

Those "information kiosks" with the touchpads meant for the
semi-literate are a poor substitute for being aware of the world the
way readers are.

But then I see an ever-widening gap between the elite and the
masses....and I think this is a good thing.

It's why I'm an Extropian.

